  herbert-q40   (78 j., fin eos): 'Artist R.M. Harringay becomes frustrated with his static portrait of an organ-grinder, which suddenly animates into a devilish figure that critiques his lack of true artistic inspiration. After a physical struggle in which Harringay paints over the demon with enamel, he claims the canvas is now blank, though his friends remain skeptical of his tale given his history of never producing a masterpiece.'
  llama-q40pur  (79 j., fin eos): 'Artist R.M. Harringay becomes convinced that his painting of an Italian organ-grinder has come to life and is mocking his lack of artistic inspiration, leading to a physical struggle where he attempts to paint over the moving canvas. Harringay ultimately silences the demon by covering the entire portrait with pale green enamel, leaving behind only a blank, enamelled panel as proof of his encounter.'
  ik-q40pur     (75 j., fin eos): 'Artist R.M. Harringay becomes frustrated with his static portrait of an organ-grinder, which suddenly animates into a devilish figure that critiques his lack of true inspiration. After a physical struggle in which Harringay paints over the demon with enamel, he silences the creature and is left with a blank green canvas, though he remains unable to produce a masterpiece.'
  llama-q4km    (67 j., fin eos): 'An artist named Harringay becomes frustrated with his lifeless painting of an Italian organ-grinder, which suddenly comes to life and offers him masterpieces in exchange for his soul. Harringay rejects the devil’s bargain and violently paints over the canvas with enamel, silencing the creature and leaving behind only a blank, green panel.'
