### l5-en (long, résumé) : Summarise the story in two sentences.
  herbert-q40   (88 j., fin eos): 'After a bitter, decades-long scientific feud ends with the death of his rival Professor Pawkins, celebrated entomologist Hapley retreats to the countryside to recover, only to become obsessed with a mysterious moth that only he can see. This hallucination, which he interprets as the ghost of Pawkins, drives him to madness, resulting in his confinement in an asylum where he spends his remaining days trying to catch the invisible insect.'
  llama-q40pur  (101 j., fin eos): "After a bitter, decades-long scientific feud with Professor Pawkins ends with Pawkins' death, the victorious but mentally unmoored entomologist Hapley retreats to the countryside, where he begins to hallucinate a mysterious, unseen moth that increasingly resembles his deceased rival. Consumed by this obsession and unable to distinguish reality from his delusions, Hapley’s sanity collapses, leading to his confinement in an asylum where he remains tormented by the phantom insect he insists is a unique specimen."
  ik-q40pur     (101 j., fin eos): "After a bitter, decades-long scientific feud with Professor Pawkins ends with Pawkins' death, the victorious but mentally unmoored entomologist Hapley retreats to the countryside, where he begins to hallucinate a mysterious, unseen moth that increasingly resembles his deceased rival. Consumed by this obsession and unable to distinguish reality from his delusions, Hapley’s sanity collapses, leading to his confinement in an asylum where he remains tormented by the phantom insect he insists is a unique specimen."
